"outdated ``If-Match`` could be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:162 055b1aa323764502a612e591a7a3e086
msgid ""
"A SCIM PUT on a user whose account expires later locked the account at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:163 92bd1ebfe2e84041b8be8b7e53087caa
msgid ""
"SCIM PATCH requests that cannot be applied answer a SCIM error instead of an "
"HTTP 500 error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:165 7556e1eb24b142e1bbd01c427f44b63e
msgid ""
"The SCIM client escapes the identifiers it puts in ``externalId`` filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../references/security.rst:2 ../../CHANGES.rst:168
#: b50bace5b17c4ef681544bb6797f7fb0 0b3ca10cd66a41f1adda4e62130f70d6
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:169 dfc03052c5cb4ef9bdb26a8833c8bf51
msgid ""
"The SCIM API accepted any access token emitted by Canaille. Client tokens "
"now need a SCIM scope. User tokens only give access to their own user, with "
"the ``scim:me`` scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:172 dcea75e71a2742338c985feb2cb5fa94
msgid ""
"With SCIM, users can only modify the attributes of their ``WRITE`` ACL on "
"their own account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:174 2f28199b1e01481ba3800d1e79e4d281
msgid "The SCIM client sent the password hashes to the provisioned clients."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:175 41d1914eddd548f48080a7f49d7f47d5
msgid ""
"A client could get scopes the user never consented to. With a request "
"object, the consent page showed the scopes of the URL. With a "
"``request_uri``, the request object could change between the consent page "
"and the user answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:178 3e23f70764ad4828ae0376e992a0a04c
msgid ""
"OIDC request objects are only downloaded from the ``request_uris`` the "
"client registered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:180 322cadce8a3f455d8e7a7fe007a4ad81
msgid ""
"Request objects and client key sets, downloaded at the ``request_uri`` and "
"``jwks_uri`` addresses clients indicate, had no size limit. They are now "
"limited to 64kB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../CHANGES.rst:183 7b0afd0a33384e698d0198bf1bed3b6e
msgid ""
"The consent page accepted answers without CSRF token. Another website could "
"make a user consent to an application."
msgstr ""

