#: ../howtos/provisioning.rst:2 08b900863e1142e896bdf0b53a6937c3
msgid "Provisioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/provisioning.rst:4 2f87785e7e89460299803cd8962d2d5c
msgid ""
"Canaille partially implement the :rfc:`SCIM <7642>` provisioning protocol, "
"so user and group modifications can be spread across an entire application "
"ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/provisioning.rst:7 0a71a4bd823b45c19d6c0e1d31a6aa65
msgid "Provisioning server"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/provisioning.rst:9 1dc09d0a570e4460957efa2ba575bffc
msgid ""
"Canaille acts as a provisioning server. This means that client applications "
"can perform requests on the ``/scim/v2`` endpoint, using the SCIM2 protocol, "
"to manage user and group objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/provisioning.rst:13 cc41c391be604da9b8b4bc9915174df6
msgid "Provisioning client"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/provisioning.rst:15 d93d9a2cc6a9479f99ee576e5d90b708
msgid ""
"Canaille also acts as a provisioning client. It sends the user and group "
"modifications to the client applications that implement a SCIM server. The "
"modifications are sent whether they come from the :ref:`web interface "
