#: ../howtos/sso.rst:96 77f3f3561b1b4afb902b2f00c4ffa6e7
msgid ""
"Users with the "
"right :attr:`~canaille.core.configuration.Permission.MANAGE_OIDC` permission "
"can manage OIDC clients through the web interface. Users with "
"the :attr:`~canaille.core.configuration.Permission.MANAGE_OWN_CLIENTS` "
"permission can create and manage their own clients. This permission is not "
"granted by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:100 6ad6cc7ba040445ab63055ff9f2b764a
msgid ""
"Here are some details about the fields in the client edition and "
"registration form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:103 5706c1ab60404e97b3a330c366c71de5
msgid "Owners"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:105 93720212035c45cf8fa5036c997b55d5
msgid ""
"The users or groups who own this client. Clients can be owned by users or "
"groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:108 083c582d31bc474693c2cdd252b37774
msgid "**User owners** can edit and use the client for authentication."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:109 d5aef4fbe8b84a12a94ad08f9c8de544
msgid ""
"**Group owners** have a distinct semantic: the *owners of the group* can "
"edit the client configuration, while *group members* can use it for "
"authentication."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:110 acb8b779c3b246f3b0a1baeda19fec6f
msgid ""
"**Global clients** (no owners) are accessible to all users with "
"the :attr:`~canaille.core.configuration.Permission.USE_OIDC` permission."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:114 bdec9cca295243a2b9220208d4b97a35
msgid ""
"Owners follow the LDAP ``owner`` attribute (:rfc:`4519#section-2.21`): they "
"are the users and groups responsible for the client. No OAuth, OpenID "
"Connect or SCIM specification defines who can use a client. Restricting a "
"client to its owners and to the members of its owner groups is a Canaille "
"extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:121 c16eb73677d84981a270ff5654121f61
msgid ""
"To restrict a client to the members of a group, add the group as an owner. "
"The owners of the group can then edit the client, if they have "
"the :attr:`~canaille.core.configuration.Permission.MANAGE_OWN_CLIENTS` "
"permission. For instance, they can change the redirect URIs, renew the "
"secret, or delete the client. Users who already consented to the client are "
"not asked again after such changes. The owners of the group also choose its "
"members, and so who can use the client. They can also make other members "
"owners of the group. When the group is deleted, the clients it is the last "
"owner of are deleted too. Only add a group whose owners you trust to manage "
"the client."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:131 869f076c0714479a80ead54645d9442a
msgid ""
"Users who cannot manage all clients can only share the clients they own with "
"the groups they own. A group owner only gets rights on the clients of the "
"group with "
"the :attr:`~canaille.core.configuration.Permission.MANAGE_OWN_GROUPS` "
"permission. They cannot add other users, nor remove the owners they do not "
"control, nor lose the edition of the client. They cannot add themselves back "
"after they left a client. They can only pick the clients they can edit as "
"token audiences. They can only add the scopes that users consent to, such as "
"``profile`` or ``email``. They cannot create access tokens without a user."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:139 bd8af780b22b44529241e726202a58fa
msgid "Clients with owners have some restrictions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:141 546dc79fe30c4d21bbaba0515c0684db
msgid ""
"They cannot use the ``client_credentials`` and ``jwt-bearer`` grant types, "
"as those issue tokens without a user consent."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:142 3481a8a87df94f4488186928b2628686
msgid ""
"They are never trusted, so they always display the consent page, even on "
"a :attr:`~canaille.oidc.configuration.OIDCSettings.TRUSTED_DOMAINS` domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:143 24fb17586fbd4f349f7ce8b39fbc2342
msgid "When the last owner of a client is deleted, the client is deleted too."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:144 535919b1cb904f02ac9fbb474144ef13
msgid ""
"Users who cannot use the client get an error, and are not redirected to the "
"client."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/sso.rst:145 280f72b736b143db991722ad111deb26
msgid ""
